.TH DISKFORMAT 1M UniSoft
.SH NAME
diskformat - format a disk
.SH SYNOPSIS
diskformat [-size #] [-dens #] [-cyl f[-t]] \
[-sec f[-t]] [-i] #] device
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Diskformat
initializes a hard disk or floppy disk and
formats it according to your specifications.
.PP
The following parameters may be specified ("device" is required):
.TP "\w'\fB\-head #[\-#]\fR\ \ 'u"
.B device
device to be formatted (must be raw device)
.TP
.B \-size #
specify sector size in bytes
.TP
.B \-dens #
specify density
.TP
.B \-cyl #[\-#]
format cylinders
.I f
to
.I t
(default 
.I f
).
A specification such as
.B \#-
means "until the end".
.TP
.B \-head #[\-#]
Format heads
.I f
to
.I t
(default
.I f
).
A specification such as
.B \#-
means "until the end".
.TP
.B \-sec #[-#]
Format sectors
.I f
to
.I t
(default
.I f
).
A specification such as
.B \#-
means "until the end".
.TP
.B \-il #
Interleave factor for the disk.
.SH EXAMPLE
.IP
.nf
diskformat /dev/rfdc0 -dens 1 -size 128 -il 3
.fi
.PP
will format the floppy disk on drive 0, single density,
128 bytes per sector with an interleave factor of 3.
This format is the only truly portable floppy format.
.\"	@(#)diskformat.1m	5.1 of 10/21/83
